            "result_text": "I've created `/app/filter.py` with a script that removes JavaScript from HTML files using three regex patterns:\n\n1. **Removes `<script>` tags** — Eliminates entire script blocks including their content\n2. **Removes event handler attributes** — Strips `onclick`, `onerror`, `onload`, and any other `on*` attributes with their values\n3. **Removes `javascript:` URLs** — Replaces dangerous protocol URLs in `href`, `src`, `action`, and similar attributes with empty strings\n\nThe script preserves:\n- All HTML structure and tags\n- Normal content and text\n- Standard attributes (class, id, style, data-*, etc.)\n- Formatting and whitespace\n\nUsage: `python filter.py <html_file>`\n\nThe file is modified in-place, so your original is overwritten with the sanitized version."
